# 3. IMPORTANT MUSIC INTEGRATION REQUIREMENT

Do not confuse YouTube Music with the YouTube Data API or the YouTube IFrame Player API.

There is no general-purpose public YouTube Music playback API that permits this application to freely control the YouTube Music app and stream its full catalogue through an arbitrary custom player.

Implement playback through the official YouTube IFrame Player API.

Official documentation:

https://developers.google.com/youtube/iframe_api_reference

https://developers.google.com/youtube/player_parameters

The music implementation must follow the applicable YouTube API Services Terms, developer policies, branding requirements and player requirements.

Specifically:

- Use the official supported embedded player.
- Do not download, extract, proxy or separately stream YouTube audio.
- Do not bypass advertisements, geographic restrictions, age restrictions or playback restrictions.
- Do not misrepresent a YouTube video as a directly hosted audio file.
- Do not create a fake player that only changes its displayed song title.
- Do not assume that a video is playable merely because its URL is valid.
- Do not conceal required YouTube attribution or branding.
- Do not remove required player functionality or obstruct the YouTube player's required controls.
- Do not use deprecated player parameters in an attempt to hide YouTube branding.
- Do not attempt to bypass minimum embedded-player dimensions or other display requirements.
- Do not assume that playback can start automatically with sound.
- Support user-initiated playback when browser autoplay policies require it.
- Provide clear error handling for unavailable, restricted or non-embeddable videos.

The custom interface may complement the official embedded player only to the extent permitted by current YouTube requirements.

If the required official player experience conflicts with the desired compact Spotify-style bar, prioritise compliance and working playback. Provide a well-designed, integrated player area rather than breaking the official player.

Do not claim to have implemented the YouTube Music API.

Do not fabricate playback, seek or duration functionality.

